        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Although octagons are the typical motif in carpets and bag faces from western Central Asia, some pieces have distinctly floral patterns. Many of these stylised flowers have been woven with light purple silk.  Silk reflects light in a different way to wool, adding lustre to the pile, but it has no functional advantage. It is, of course, expensive and therefore is a visible way of showing affluence."@en ;
